From: OpenStack Incus maintainers <openstack-incus@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] compute: Schedule Manila migrations by capability

Nova rejects every live migration, cold migration, and resize when an
instance has a share mapping. The Incus driver can pre-mount the share on
the destination and unmount it on the source after handoff.

Require the source resource provider to advertise the operation-specific
capability. Add that same trait to RequestSpec.root_required so Placement
only returns capable destination providers. The legacy forced live migration
path bypasses the scheduler, so validate its explicit destination provider
directly. Other actions, drivers, and Incus nodes remain blocked.

Also reject share attach/detach while an instance task is active and expose
small ComputeManager transaction hooks for destination preparation, access
revocation, and rollback completion. The base hooks are no-ops, so existing
drivers retain their behavior while an out-of-tree manager can keep Manila
mount ownership and migration task state ordered durably.

